WEBVTT

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:04.940
The third round of Pantasia´s
customary newcomers’ battle has begun.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.440
Kazuma was facing off against
the mysterious masked baker, Koala.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.070
All right!

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.630
Azuma.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.410
I won’t lose.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.250
Amazing!

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.660
It’s a dragon whichever way you look at it.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.800
This is what Koala-chan’s true skill is...

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.300
Give up on being the successor, okay, onee-san?

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.720
To fight the dragon bread
created by the man

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.810
that Matsushiro believes to be
Japan’s #1 braided bread artisan,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.730
the bread that Kazuma made was...

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.510
a turtle!

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.780
It’s done!

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:42.900
Ma...

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.110
It’s magic!

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.600
The baked bread is...

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.030
It’s all green.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.330
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.210
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.540
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.030
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:11.180
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.060
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:32.150
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:40.120
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:47.960
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:55.710
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:03.180
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:12.560
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:21.320
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.580
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.540
is the light of only you.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:32.320
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.130
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:44.850
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.480
The great decisive battle!!

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.160
Koala’s dragon vs. Kazuma’s turtle!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.080
What’s going on here?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.420
If it was the dough inside, I’d understand...

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.580
But once you bake bread, the
surface just has to become brown.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.760
And to be able to bake it so that it’s so very green...

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.970
I can’t think of anything
except that Azuma really used magic.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.690
You want to know the trick behind Azuma’s magic?

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.480
That is...

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.060
A technique known as Super-Low Temperature, Ultra-Long Time Calcination!!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.270
Calcination: to heat (a substance) to a high temperature but below the melting or fusing point, causing loss of moisture and reduction or oxidation.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.560
Super-Low Temperature,
Ultra-Long Time Calcination?!

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.320
Normally, such sweet breads are
baked at 200°C to 220°C.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.990
And it goes without saying that
the surface burns until it’s brown.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.240
But...

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.460
If you set the temperature of the oven to
the Super-Low value of below 150°C,

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.660
the bread does not char.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.750
The dark green dough will not turn brown and

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.080
will not change dimensions after being baked.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.210
But then,

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.050
in exchange for baking at low temperatures, you have to bake it for a longer time.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.050
Is that so?

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.140
That’s why Azuma had...

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.590
Not yet.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.710
Some more.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.140
More.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.720
Some more.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.740
...baked the bread for so long.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.110
What’s this moody breeze?

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.410
Hearts?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.060
Oh my.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:24.950
That Dave, who would only say,
“Aaah, so busy, so busy,” is...

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.780
And on top of that he’s turned bright red.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.460
Dave is in love.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:30.960
What?

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.680
The only emotion Dave has left,
other than an appetite, is...

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:36.930
It is...

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:37.840
It is...?!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.210
A love for... food!!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.720
Love?!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.970
Love, he says!!

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.440
Koala’s dragon bread and Azuma’s turtle bread.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.930
It’s proof that he’s come across two
brand-new, delicious looking beauties.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.480
Is that so?

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.780
I... I don’t quite understand, but...

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.480
either way, a life where your lover is a piece of bread...

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.480
is one that I really don’t want.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.660
Yes. This is wonderful!

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.990
As a baker, I’ve seen many
different breads in the past, but...

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.250
the molding of the dragon is a marvel.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.790
And the addition of color to the turtle is amazing.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.960
I’ve been presented with high-level skills and techniques.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:17.710
You both receive full marks, that
is, 10 points, on artistic presentation.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.960
They drew on the artistic presentation, huh?

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.970
The hard part begins now, Azuma.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.190
You appear to have prolonged
your life here for a little longer, but...

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.110
now comes the taste test.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.480
Koala-chan will definitely not lose.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.350
Kazu-kun...

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.360
Well then.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.100
We’ll now begin judging the taste, so...

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.700
Everyone within the kitchen, please
take care of your ears.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:43.620
Huh?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:44.950
Ears?

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.570
Here you go, Assistant Haijima.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:51.580
Dave.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.540
It’s time for lunch.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.540
Okay, we start with the dragon.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:02.970
She’s a meshi-stant rather than an assistant, isn’t she?

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.670
If we keep it within our industry...

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.150
That fatso...
He can’t even eat on his own?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:12.740
What the...?
There seems to be a lot of activity there.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.410
What in the...?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:20.600
Umm...

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.470
225 points!

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.130
Yes!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.340
A new record!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.550
What?!

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.050
This is the...

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.390
Devil Horn War Cry.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.180
It’s a variety of war cry!!

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.800
Dave expresses the
deliciousness of an item by screaming.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.940
Tiny differences in deliciousness
can be measured by war cry points...

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.810
This is the reason he’s considered a
more discerning judge than Kuroyanagi.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.610
It’s a fearsome judgment.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.780
My eardrums almost burst.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.830
And by the way, the best
record of last year’s winner was...

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:11.820
180 points.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.020
In other words, the dragon
bread scored surprisingly high.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.710
What?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.890
Then, aren’t we in some real trouble here?

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:34.640
Wh-What?!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.810
Tha... That is...

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.610
The star of Kung-fu movies...

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:38.690
Dragon!

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:43.020
Don’t tell me... Kuro-yan is having a “dragon reaction” after eating the dragon bread...!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.530
But... Why on the ceiling...?

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.040
The orange marmalade poured on the surface has

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.320
been just faintly singed, leaving a fleeting astringency

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.210
and a combination of a rich sweet and tart taste.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.050
And on top of that the
spaces in between the netted scales

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.640
have little bits of chocolate saying hello to you!

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.260
The orange and chocolate
complement each other perfectly!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.970
This can definitely be called an
animal bread that even adults can enjoy!

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.400
Without doubt, a taste that
can transport you to the heavens.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.600
Amazing.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.190
You may say heaven.
But that’s just the ceiling...

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:22.980
There...

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.780
I may be talking puns here, but...

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.360
Kuroyanagi’s reaction from Koala’s bread is tremendous.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.980
This is bad...

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.580
You’re all right, aren’t you, Azuma...?

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:36.990
Your Super-Low temperature,
Ultra-Long time calcination thing...

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:38.790
Come to think of it, Manager...

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.210
Even if the appearance of
something made by Super-Low temperature,

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.050
Ultra-Long time calcination is fantastic...

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.630
how does it taste?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:46.250
Without doubt, it’s outrageously delicious, right?

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.220
It’s disgusting.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.380
What?

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:53.520
Bread typically made by Super-Low temperature, Ultra-Long time calcination is disgusting.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:57.440
The longer it’s baked, the lower the
water content gets, making it dry.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.980
That’s why nobody does it, normally.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.190
What?

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:05.350
If you knew that then why didn’t you stop him?

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:11.120
He can’t possibly be awarded any points for a bad bread even if it looks good on the outside.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.450
Who said that Azuma’s bread is disgusting?

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:14.360
What?

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.500
I just said that bread typically made by

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:19.870
Super-Low temperature, Ultra-Long time calcination is disgusting.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.120
What’s he talking about?
What could he mean?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.340
And to proceed, we will now
judge Azuma Kazuma’s bread.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:26.340
All right!

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.960
Haijima-san! Please do the honors.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.680
Azuma! Give me the bread as well.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.050
Huh? Sure, but how?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.730
Please...

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.520
Almost there...

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.520
All right, stop.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.190
Just as I thought.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.400
This has been prepared by Super-Low
temperature, Ultra-Long time calcination,

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.570
which is the reason that the brilliant color has remained.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.620
If you make use of this technique,

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:56.570
the bread definitely loses some taste due to loss of water content.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.460
Did you try to win points for just artistic presentation in spite of knowing that?

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:01.950
What?

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.380
It’s your decision as to what you do, but...

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.420
there will be nothing further to
talk about should it taste bad!

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.880
Exactly, Kazu-kun.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.370
There’s no meaning to it if it tastes bad.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.250
Are you prepared?!

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.340
Yeah!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.050
Here you go, Dave.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.040
225 points!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.670
It’s exactly the same as Koala’s dragon-bread.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:44.870
A draw?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.340
No, wait!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.760
It depends on Kuro-yan’s reaction.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.880
Wh-What’s this sound?

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.450
What is it...?

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.570
This sound was made by... Kuro-yan?!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:20.910
What the...?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.080
Oh, Jesus!

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:29.970
He’s spinning like crazy!

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.050
But, what’s this?!

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.000
Can’t you see it?!

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.590
I can see it.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.170
Right now, he’s truly become...

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.570
the monster from outer space...

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.200
He’s Gamera!

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:48.610
Gamera

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.320
The emperor of all turtles!
Space monster Gamera!
Gamera

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.560
It’s an indigenous Kadokawa film!
Gamera

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.040
Kuroyanagi’s midair decisive battle
It’s an indigenous Kadokawa film!
Gamera

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.990
Gamera
Kuroyanagi’s midair decisive battle

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.950
I wonder if it’s okay with copyright to do such things.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.290
If you do Super-Low
temperature, Ultra-Long time calcination,

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:08.170
you can create a bread that doesn’t turn brown and remains the color of the original dough!

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.950
Yeah... exactly.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.920
But, in exchange for that, due
to being baked for a long time,

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.680
the dough loses water content and
ends up having a dry texture to it!

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:17.640
However!

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.920
This bread is almost overflowing with moisture.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:24.220
It deserves to be called the emperor of all turtle breads!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:28.220
It’s powerful stuff, the turtle bread.
Is it powerful stuff, the turtle bread?

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.720
It’s delicious! This turtle bread!

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:34.230
Kazuma! You’ve used starch syrup here, haven’t you?

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:34.650
Yeah...

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.230
Congratulations on having
come up with such a concept!

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.290
That was...

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:46.000
Is it okay, old man with a scary face?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:46.870
Yeah.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.250
At a stall, during a neighborhood festival,

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:54.090
I was given a candied apple that remained unsold.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.370
It’s really good...

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.130
It was pretty old, yet...

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:01.380
The apple inside was still really moist.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:05.390
So, learning that apples surrounded
by starch syrup didn’t dry out,

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:08.900
I applied it to bread.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:14.020
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.520
Is what I’d like to say, but...

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.610
the wonder of Koala’s bread can’t be denied either.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:26.610
This is further proved by Dave-sensei’s phonetic points.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:27.490
Therefore...

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.490
It’s a draw!
We will have another battle.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:34.830
This way, I get to eat
yet another delicious bread.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.290
That won’t do.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:38.670
The Koala speaks!

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.420
Wh-What?!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.670
You’re discontent with the draw?!

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.350
That’s right.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:46.980
It’s my loss.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.640
There can’t possibly be a draw.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.970
Ko... Koala-chan!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.770
Mr. Judge.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.940
While I may be a newcomer at Pantasia,

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.520
my career as a baker is far from that of a newcomer.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:03.120
I’m a person who’s even worked as the
manager of a certain famous bakery.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.160
In other words...

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.250
I’m a person who shouldn’t
really even be at such a competition.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.530
That’s why I threw away the appearance of a human and took on the Boss’s beloved...

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.030
A koala, huh?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:15.040
But, truth be told, the newcomers’
battle should be between newcomers.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.590
I’m tired of pretending to be something I’m not.

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.540
Therefore...

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.560
I wish to forfeit.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.540
Koala...

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.520
Mokoyama...

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.350
Your identity has been taken
into account from the very start.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:28.980
But!

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:31.850
As long as you’ve been
acknowledged as a newcomer by Pantasia,

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.400
anybody has the right to participate.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.940
Whether you be an animal, or a talking animal.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.900
And, this goes without saying,
you too, Koala!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.070
Is that so...?

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:44.160
That’s why it was okay with Katsuo as well.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.780
Thank you, Mr. Judge.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.700
But, for now, as a member of Pantasia,

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.250
if I was to really think about Pantasia’s interests...

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.840
Rather than a person like me
with no future,

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:01.710
I believe that this wonderful young man here should be the one to proceed to the semifinals.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.390
Do as you please.
I won’t say any more.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.050
I give you leave to do as you will.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.230
And I thought that I’d be able to
eat yet another delicious bread, but...

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:14.980
In that case... Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.350
No way...

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.740
You’ve become even stronger, haven’t you?

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:27.360
To think that I lost at the subject I’m strongest at...

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.210
It’s your complete victory.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.790
Don’t make such a face.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.340
In truth, I bore a grudge against you.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:37.590
When we drew in the challenge on television,

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:39.870
I was really frustrated.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:41.410
10 points...

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:42.460
10 points...

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:43.680
10 points!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.710
A perfect score!

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.670
This is mortifying!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.480
Thanks to that, I got fired...

00:15:58.110 --> 00:15:59.740
I became Koala...

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.940
But, you know...

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:07.070
Thanks to that frustration, I was able to
bring back my old self that I’d forgotten.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:09.830
I stopped going to beauty and nail salons and...

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.330
I remembered the person
within who took his bread seriously.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:16.980
I remembered how I’d get excited over
making bread and over trying to beat my rival.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:19.540
Just like a newcomer...

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.430
Koala... No, old man Mokoyama.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.020
It’s all right.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.550
Leaving that aside, I have a request for you all.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.980
If may just be the selfish wish of a koala, but...

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.560
In truth the match was a draw, so...

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.910
can’t the bet with Boss be ignored?

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.740
What?

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.950
No, that’s...

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:47.270
Of course.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:49.410
Huh? Tsukino...

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.610
At that time...

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.250
She’s scary, Kazu-kun.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:56.160
Kazu-kun?

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.660
By doing something like that,
my employee will again be...

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.660
You thieving cat.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.660
Thieving cat?

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:06.920
Isn’t that your mother?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.340
Stop, Tsukino!

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:12.340
That hurt!

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.340
No way!

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:17.390
I-I’m sorry. I...

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.400
Tsukino, you idiot!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.270
Siblings should get along well together.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:28.080
I regret not being very mature myself at that time.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:30.870
We’re sisters, and should not be competing against each other,

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.830
or quarreling with each other.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:37.880
I don’t think that Grandfather
wishes for such a thing, either.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.660
And,

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:44.660
no matter how much she hates me,
Mizuno is my one and only little sister.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.140
SHUT UP!!

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:52.100
Shut up, shut up, shut up!!!

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.680
Everyone, stop saying whatever you please.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.020
You no longer have the right to be my pet.

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:57.720
You’re fired!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.680
I understand, Boss.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.980
It’s just that... I’ll leave you with just one warning.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:07.890
At this rate, Pantasia will be crushed by St. Pierre.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:12.490
There’s no end to the ambition of St. Pierre’s owner.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:15.420
He’s just waiting for a chance to take it all over.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.410
If Pantasia is having internal strife, then...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.670
someday, you will lose it all.

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:24.660
Just keep that in mind.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:26.120
Boss...

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.630
Thank you for employing trash like me.

00:18:32.390 --> 00:18:35.130
It was fun.
Like I had a daughter of my own.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.180
Is it okay, Mizuno?

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.240
He’s going away.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.700
Mokoyama-san.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:53.070
If may not be my place to say this, but...

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:57.330
You may never again find a
replacement for that man in this lifetime.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.700
Tsukino, in that case, why don’t we
employ him for cheap at our place?

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.330
He’s a newcomer after all...

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.790
We can pay him a lower
salary than Azuma and the rest.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:05.960
Let’s see...

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:07.880
How about this much?

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.550
You’re going to pay Koala that much?

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:10.710
But...

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.420
This level should be just fine, just fine...

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.800
Kawachi-san, that’s pushing it too far.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.550
He’s going to be sleeping and
staying on the 2nd floor of the store.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.300
It should be just fine with this.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.390
I really don’t want to be living
under the same roof as that old man.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.270
I’m also completely against it.

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:26.030
Shut UP!

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.320
Just watch.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.640
We won’t lose next time.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:32.650
Onee-chan.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:36.570
And St. Pierre is no challenge either.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.080
Mama!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.040
Don’t look.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.130
It’s a koala! A koala.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.080
Let’s go.
It’s a koala! A koala.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.630
It’s a lovely day.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.580
It’s been a while since I felt like this.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.590
It’s like being fashion-conscious
is a thing of the distant past.

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:07.700
Losing to that boy, and losing my job...

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:13.100
But, once my eyes were opened,
I was able to start my training again.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.180
It was then that...

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.880
Boss found me.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.220
You were abandoned?

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:39.560
Want to come over to us?

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.570
There it is!

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:49.600
Here you go!

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.060
Meeting Boss...

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.060
Spending time together with her...

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.990
It really felt like I had a daughter.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.380
I was happy.

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:08.420
But...

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.080
even that is now over.

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:14.140
It can’t be helped.
You reap as you sow.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:31.200
Koala-chan!

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:38.790
Koala-chan!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.230
Where are you?

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.740
Boss!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.500
Okay, so I take back firing you!

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:05.350
I won’t forgive you if you go off
anywhere on your own.

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:07.720
You’re to work at our store!

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:14.160
Thank you, Boss.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:19.110
She’s really a kid with no consistency.

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:20.230
It’s good this way.

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.980
You’ve met with a good boss, haven’t you, Mokoyama?

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:27.490
Mizuno, let’s work hard, shall we?

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:32.420
You really, really better not go
anywhere, okay, Koala-chan?

00:22:32.420 --> 00:22:34.260
It’s an order, okay?

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:07.130
Next, it’s my turn!

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:10.160
I’ll prepare an even more extravagant bread than the turtle-shaped monster from outer space.

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:11.340
Wait and watch, Azuma!

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:12.170
Manager!

00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:13.330
And Tsukino!

00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:14.590
Eh? Tsukino’s not here.

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:15.460
Where did she go?

00:24:15.460 --> 00:24:17.090
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:17.090 --> 00:24:19.130
With a little prayer!!
An oath on the grave!

00:24:19.130 --> 00:24:20.020
Be sure to see it!

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:22.770
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:23.710
Kazuma used starch syrup!

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:24.430
Starch syrup
Kazuma used starch syrup!

00:24:24.430 --> 00:24:27.220
The history of starch syrup
dates back to Japan’s very earliest days.

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:28.560
The root of the word “ame” is “sweet.”

00:24:28.560 --> 00:24:29.890
The root of the word for “delicious” is also “sweet.”

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:31.750
Therefore, rain is delicious!

00:24:32.100 --> 00:24:33.900
Really?!
